^#^
describe^#^
SUBTOPIC-player^#^
                    -=[ Help ]=-

       command: describe
        Usuage: describe

   Description: describe allows you to make a description of
                yourself.  This description will be seen when
                other players look at you.

Related topics: finger.
 
^#^
do^#^
SUBTOPIC-player^#^
                    -=[ Help ]=-

       command: do
        Usuage: do command1, command2, command3, etc, etc

   Description: The do command is an online macro command.  It
                is here to put everyone on the same par, as some
                users have this facility and others don't.  The do
                command will parse through command1, command2, etc.
                If any command fails it will abort the 'do'.  One
                special command available to 'do' is the 'wait'
                command.  A delay of 1 to 30 secs can be made before
                the next command is made.  If the do command is too
                large, you may get evaluation errors.

       Example: do north, fireball, wait 10, south 

Related topics: alias.
 
^#^
drop^#^
SUBTOPIC-player^#^
                    -=[ Help ]=-

       command: drop
        Usuage: drop <item> in <container>
                drop all in <container>
                drop <item>
                drop all
                drop <amount> coins
   Description: This allows you to drop an item, or all items
                from your inventory.  Some items, once picked 
                up cannot be dropped.  This maybe because it
                is a special creator item, or it might even be
                cursed.

Related topics: get, give, put, inventory.
 
^#^
debug^#^
SUBTOPIC-creator^#^
                    -=[ Help ]=-

       command: debug
        Usuage: debug

   Description: debug tails the runtime error log file.

Related topics: log, main, rlog.
 
^#^
deltree^#^
SUBTOPIC-creator^#^
                    -=[ Help ]=-

       command: deltree
        Usuage: deltree <full pathname>

   Description: This command allows you to delete all of a directory
                tree.  Be careful that there is no files you wish to
                keep in the directory tree.

Related topics: rm, mkdir, rmdir.
 
^#^
dest^#^
SUBTOPIC-creator^#^
                    -=[ Help ]=-

       command: dest
        Usuage: dest <item(s)>

   Description: This command destructs all of item(s).  Item(s) can be
                any object(s) referenced by the object parser.  *** It
                will only destruct interactive players if they are
                referenced directly. *** 

       Example: dest zilanthius   /* works - but can lead to demotion */
                dest users        /* fails */

Related topics: parser, dest, bomb.
 
^#^
domain^#^
SUBTOPIC-creator^#^
                    -=[ Help ]=-

       command: domain
        Usuage: domain <domain> <who> <level>

   Description: If domain does not exist, "who" will be made the domain
                lord.  They have complete file access control over their
                domain and can promote anyone in their domain.  If
                domain already exists a directory, and file access
                objects are added to domain for "who".  Only arches can
                create new domains.

Related topics: promote.
 
^#^
dup^#^
SUBTOPIC-creator^#^
                    -=[ Help ]=-

       command: duplicate
        Usuage: duplicate <item(s)>
                duplicate <item(s)::destination(s)>
                dup <item(s)>
                dup <item(s)::destination(s)>

   Description: This command allows you clone an item(s) and move them
                to a destination(s).  The default destination is the
                creator.  item and destination can be any object(s) that
                can be referenced using the object parser.

Related topics: clone, parser.
 
^#^
dark elf^#^
SUBTOPIC-races^#^
     ::: Dark Elves :::

Dark elves, also known as drow, are the most divergent of the
elven sub-races. Their form is similar to that of other elves,
but their skin colour is the inky black of a moonless night and
their hair is normally pure white or silver. Drow are generally
evil and chaotic in nature, though some outcasts are known not
to be. Drow shun the light and rarely venture forth accept on the
gloomiest and most overcast of days. Drow society is run by the
women, and thus, they are the most powerful of their race. Drow
worship Lolth; the Demon Queen of Spiders; and are excelent
clerics, fighters, and thieves. Usually, the men of this society
become mages as the women are the ones that are permitted to
advance and gain the most power in clerical circles. However,
their skills are also watched carefully by the women, and are not
permitted to become more powerful than they are.

As a player you receive an added weapon class bonus for using weapons
in both hands. Players dark elves are able to find things more easily
when they search rooms, as they have more hightened senses than other 
races. As player dark elves are exposed to sunlight, they lose their
other magical powers, such as innate magic resistance, and the spell
casting they were taught as children.


